;; E5 finding: agy's terminal tool allocates a PTY for every command ("failed to create PTY: operation not permitted" without this).
;; Minimal: these file rules alone suffice; `(allow pseudo-tty)` alone does not. COST: the regex covers every pseudo-terminal of the machine, including the owner's own terminals (owner-owned, mode 620): a builder worker could read or write another terminal. Not narrowed in the spike (the Step cannot know its ttys in advance); open for the adapter.
;; Only needed in the builder shape (shell); the reviewer-readonly shape has no shell and so no PTY.
(allow file-read* file-write* file-ioctl (literal "/dev/ptmx") (regex #"^/dev/ttys[0-9]+$"))
